<span id="S3.T1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T1.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Endpoint Detection and Response/AntiVirus (EDR/AV) KILLERS</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S3.T1.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T1.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Evades detection and disables security mechanisms on endpoints using techniques like process injection, obfuscation, persistence, and process termination.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S3.T1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T1.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RANSOMWARE</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S3.T1.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T1.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Encrypts a victim’s files, rendering the data inaccessible. Attacker then demands a ransom payment, typically in cryptocurrency, in exchange for the decryption key.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S3.T1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T1.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T1.2.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RAT - REMCOS Family</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
